{"name":"Dingy Sticky Note","hex":"#e6f2a2","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dingy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Dark, dull.","Shabby, squalid, uncared-for."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of dinghy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dingy"},{"term":"sticky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tending to stick; able to adhere via the drying of a viscous substance.","Difficult, awkward."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sticky note, such as a post-it note.","A discussion thread fixed at the top of the list of topics or threads so as to keep it in view."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sticky"},{"term":"note","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A symbol or annotation.","A written or printed communication or commitment."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To notice with care; to observe; to remark; to heed.","To record in writing; to make a memorandum of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/note"}],"entries":[{"title":"Post-it note","blocks":[{"text":"A Post-it note is a small piece of paper with a re-adherable strip of glue on its back, made for temporarily attaching notes to documents and other surfaces. A low-tack pressure-sensitive adhesive allows the notes to be easily attached, removed, and even re-posted elsewhere without leaving residue. The Post-it's signature adhesive was discovered accidentally by a scientist at 3M. Originally small yellow squares, Post-it notes and related products are available in various colors, shapes, sizes, and adhesive strengths. As of 2024, there are at least 28 documented colors of Post-it notes. 3M's Post-it has won several awards for its design and innovation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Post-it-2020.svg/330px-Post-it-2020.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Post-it_note","wikidata":"Q181331"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/PostItNotePad.JPG/500px-PostItNotePad.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/PostItNotePad.JPG/500px-PostItNotePad.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APostItNotePad.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Fry-lightbulb-on-forehead1.jpg/500px-Fry-lightbulb-on-forehead1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Fry-lightbulb-on-forehead1.jpg/500px-Fry-lightbulb-on-forehead1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Arthur Fry, developer of the Post-it note","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFry-lightbulb-on-forehead1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Post-it_note_adhesive.jpg/500px-Post-it_note_adhesive.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Post-it_note_adhesive.jpg/500px-Post-it_note_adhesive.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The adhesive side of a Post-it note, magnified 555 times with a scanning electron microscope","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APost-it_note_adhesive.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Klaus_Theweleit_W71_01.jpg/500px-Klaus_Theweleit_W71_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Klaus_Theweleit_W71_01.jpg/1280px-Klaus_Theweleit_W71_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org